		(uuid "a9d76286-5806-4207-bf1c-f51ca79f8afb")
	)
	(text_box "PIN ASSIGNMENT METHODOLOGY:\nSource: Lattice ECP5 caBGA381 pin migration data (per-device column), this spreadsheet confirms bank, dual function, and differential status for any physical ball.\n\nRefer to bank/voltage map first - confirms what's already committed before hunting for a free pin.\n\nBefore assigning a pin, check:\n   - bank: must match the voltage already committed to that bank\n   - dual Function: some balls double as clock inputs - don't collide\n   - differential: only matters if building an actual diff pair (see\n     A/B vs +/- note)\n\nBefore wiring any IC's pins, verify against its own datasheet, never assume a reference design's values/pins carry over to a different part or voltage combo.\n\nUnused pin default = NC (no connect). No external pull resistor needed (see \"UNUSED GPIO PINS\" note). Only add one if the FPGA's internal pull is intentionally disabled in the constraints file.\nUNUSED GPIO PINS:\nUnused ordinary GPIOs are left as No Connect - no external\npull resistor required. The ECP5 has internal weak pulls enabled\nby default on every I/O (tri-stated with weak pull-down at power-up).\nOnly add an external pull if the internal one is intentionally\ndisabled in the pin constraints file.\nSource: Lattice Answer Database #738.\n\nGPDI DIFFERENTIAL SIGNALING:\nGPDI does NOT use the ECP5's dedicated True-LVDS hardware driver.\nIt uses \"emulated\" differential signaling - ordinary LVCMOS pins\ndriven as a complementary pair, using external resistors/caps to\napproximate the signal levels. This works on any confirmed A/B pin\npair, True-LVDS-flagged or not, and needs no special 2.5V bank.\nSource: Lattice ECP5 sysI/O Usage Guide, FPGA-TN-02032.\n\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.304 89.662 0)
		(size 134.874 68.072)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "14794775-4842-4449-a049-2a533a932444")
	)
	(text_box "NET LABEL NAMING CONVENTION:\nA/B suffix (ex. GPIO_14A, GPIO_14B):\nTwo pins that are physically related on the FPGA package (adjacent\npair number) but electrically INDEPENDENT, meaning each carries its own\nunrelated signal. NOT a differential pair.\n\n+/- suffix (ex GPIO_8+, GPIO_8-):\nA differential pair - the two pins are deliberately driven\nas opposites of each other to carry ONE signal. \n\nWhether a given physical pin pair is used as A/B or +/- is a design\nchoice made on the sheet where it's wired - not a fixed property of\nthe silicon. Check the destination, not just the pin name, if unsure.\n\nVOLTAGE MAP:\nBank 0   3.3V   single-ended only - GPIO expansion header \nBank 1   3.3V   GPDI video output (emulated differential) + GPIO exp.\nBank 2   3.3V   SDRAM \nBank 3   3.3V   SDRAM \nBank 6   3.3V   USB/JTAG, SD card\nBank 7   3.3V   GPIO expansion header, audio, LEDs\nBank 8   -      Dedicated config/JTAG pins (not general GPIO)\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.558 37.592 0)
		(size 134.874 46.99)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "326d4d3d-7c46-4321-834a-863880168653")
	)
	(text_box "REFERENCE DOCUMENTS USED THROUGHOUT:\nFPGA CORE\n- ECP5 and ECP5-5G Family Datasheet - FPGA-DS-02012\n- ECP5 sysI/O Usage Guide - FPGA-TN-02032\n- ECP5 Power Decoupling and Bypass Filtering App Note - FPGA-TN-02115\n- ECP5 sysCONFIG Usage Guide (TN1260) - boot mode strapping, pull-up\n  requirements, SPI flash programming\n- ECP5 Programming and Configuration Usage Guide - FPGA-TN-02050\n- ECP5 Package Diagrams (mechanical/ball pitch/diameter) - FPGA-DS-02053\n- ECP5 Pin Migration (caBGA381) - pin-level ball/bank/differential data\n- Lattice Answer Database #738 - unused I/O pin handling\n\nPER-COMPONENT DATASHEETS\n- TLV62569 (switching regulator) - design equations, Table 4 (L/C matrix)\n- MAX11120-MAX11128 (ADC family) - MAX11125 specifics, SWCNV mode\n- IS25LP128 (SPI flash)\n- IS42S16160J / MT48LC16M16A2 (SDRAM)\n- FT231XS (USB-to-UART bridge) - pin functions, CBUS defaults\n- PCA9306D (I2C level shifter) - DDC/EDID voltage translation\n- BZT52C3V6 (zener diode) - HPD clamp\n- OV7670 (camera sensor) - XCLK requirement, DVP timing\n- CUI SJ-43516-SMT-TR (audio/video jack) - pinout\n\nSTANDARDS\n- RS-170A / SMPTE 170M (composite video) - 75 ohm load impedance origin\n- USB Type-C spec - CC1/CC2 pulldown convention for legacy device mode\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
